{"strongs": "H8336", "word": "שֵׁשׁ", "translit": "shesh", "root": "שש", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "byssus", "definition": "III. שֵׁשׁ noun masculine Exod 26:1 byssus (loan-word probably from Egyptian šen-suten Reinischap. DHM VOJ viii (1894), 7 Coptic šens , compare Coptic šent , weave ; see M'Lean Ency.Bib. LINEN ; on spinning, weaving, and wearing of linen in Egypt Erman Aegypten 594 ff.; Eng. Trans. 448 f. ); — always absolute ׳ שׁ ( שׁשׁי Ezek 16:13 is error): — byssus , fine Egyptian linen ( בּוּץ , q. v., is later synonym), i.e. the linen thread (spun by women Exod 35:25 ), and the material woven from it: used for garments Gen 41:42 ( E ), Ezek 16:10 ; Ezek 16:13 ( שׁשׁי , read שׁשׁ ), Prov 31:22 for sail (in figurative of Tyre as ship) Ezek 27:7 (brought from Egypt); elsewhere P , of priestly vestments Exod 28:5 ; Exod 28:39 (twice in verse); Exod 39:3 ; Exod 39:27 ; Exod 39:28 (twice in verse); also מָשְׁזָר ׳ שׁ twisted linen Exod 28:6 ; Exod 28:8 ; Exod 28:15 ; Exod 39:2 ; Exod 39:5 ; Exod 39:8 ; Exod 39:28 ; Exod 39:29 + v Exod 39:24 (read ׳ וְשֵׁשׁ מ ⅏ ᵐ5 Bae ); ׳ שׁ of hangings, etc., in tabernacle Exod 25:4 ; Exod 35:6 ; Exod 35:23 ; Exod 35:25 ; Exod 35:35 ; Exod 38:23 , and so מָשְׁזָר ׳ שׁ Exod 26:1 ; Exod 26:31 ; Exod 26:36 ; Exod 27:9 ; Exod 27:16 ; Exod 27:18 ; Exod 36:8 ; Exod 36:35 ; Exod 36:37 ; Exod 38:9 ; Exod 38:16 ; Exod 38:18 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9063')\">BDB9063</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8336')\">H8336</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9062')\">BDB9062</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9064')\">BDB9064</entry></div><p> III. <bdbheb>שֵׁשׁ</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 26:1\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(2,26,1)\">Exod 26:1</ref></sup> <highlightword>byssus</highlightword> (loan-word probably from Egyptian <transliteration><highlight>šen-suten</highlight></tra